	-> HPA (Horizontal Pod Auto-scaling),  VPA (Vertical Pod Auto-scaling)
		- need to install metrics API first 
		- node specifications > kubectl top node
		- pod specifications > kubectl top pod
		
	-> HPA : 
		- scale pods horizontally so it scales the numbers of replica of yr pod (trigger on cpu utilization load)
		- to trigger load on yr pod > kubectl run -it load-generator --image=busybox -n apache -- /bin/sh
				 then in sh > while true; do wget -q -O- http://<svc_name>.<ns_name>.svc.cluster.local; done
		
	-> VPA :
		- scale pods vertically so it scales the cpu core of yr pod (triggers on cpu utilization load)
	
	-> node affinity : Node affinity is a Kubernetes scheduling feature that constrains which nodes a pod can be scheduled on based on node labels. It serves as a more expressive and flexible replacement for the basic nodeSelector, allowing administrators to define complex placement rules using logical operators (like In, NotIn, Exists) rather than simple exact key-value matches.
	
